<article class="env-lemma" id="0DVC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DVC">Lemma <span data-tag="0DVC">13.30.2</span>.</a> Let $F : \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ and $G : \mathcal{B} \to \mathcal{A}$ be functors of abelian categories such that $F$ is a right adjoint to $G$. Let $K^\bullet $ be a complex of $\mathcal{A}$ and let $M^\bullet $ be a complex of $\mathcal{B}$. If $RF$ is defined at $K^\bullet $ and $LG$ is defined at $M^\bullet $, then there is a canonical isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(\mathcal{B})}(M^\bullet , RF(K^\bullet )) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(\mathcal{A})}(LG(M^\bullet ), K^\bullet )  \]
</div>
  <p> This isomorphism is functorial in both variables on the triangulated subcategories of $D(\mathcal{A})$ and $D(\mathcal{B})$ where $RF$ and $LG$ are defined. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of the very general Lemma <a href="/tag/0FND" data-tag="0FND">13.30.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>